From e3b7dd31167e98cc9ef63b0a923c1c5b6e8546c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 18:24:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate Sample Collection to the shared workflow stepper
 component
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Registration, Test Order and Billing all already render their progress
trail via <lis-workflow-stepper/>, but Sample Collection still shipped
its own bespoke .proc-timeline markup/CSS/stepState() logic — despite
the shared component's own doc comment saying it was ported FROM this
page's design. This was the one page that never actually got migrated.

- Added an optional ariaLabel input to WorkflowStepperComponent so
  Sample Collection can keep its more specific 'Sample lifecycle
  progress' label instead of the generic default.
- Replaced Sample Collection's local TIMELINE_STEPS/StepState/
  stepState() duplication with the shared WorkflowStep type and
  <lis-workflow-stepper/>, wrapped in a lightweight .timeline-card
  for the framed look (the dot+connector visuals themselves now
  live in the shared component's CSS, not duplicated locally).
- Removed the now-dead .proc-* CSS block.
---
